ary picture, with progressive candidates leading early polling in neighboring New Hampshire and speculation about Bernie Sanders' political successor in Vermont. None of that suggests the general election here will be close. A Republican win would require a national environment far more hostile to Democrats than anything currently measurable. The race sits at Likely Democratic, with wide uncertainty given the absence of direct polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.967, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9556, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9811, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9288, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9351, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9368, "margin": 17.0}]}